# Evidence before changing code — always apply

Before writing any fix prompted by an error, an error-tracker event, a support ticket, or "X used
to work" — and before naming a root cause in an RCA — run the gate in
[`evidence-before-changing-code/SKILL.md`](../skills/evidence-before-changing-code/SKILL.md): a bug
report is evidence code broke, never evidence it should exist.

## Forbidden

- Treating "there's an error" as proof the erroring thing should be added back, without running the
  skill's history and in-flight-work checks first.
- Silently restoring or silently closing a report when history contradicts it — the skill's gate is
  to ask the author of the conflicting change, not to settle it unilaterally either way.
